From 012e9cab62ce2e17679f36dcb4dd737d01fe4b08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:52:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(kanban-sync): keep BoardWatch readers across WAL
 checkpoints; split the wait step's CPU live

The Mac sync loop's wait step cost 2.67 ms/round (run52), unchanged by #4023. Every WAL
checkpoint moved a board's main-file mtime and BoardWatch reopened its reader (about 3 ms of
schema parsing per board each time).

- kanban_sync_wal_evidence: read the wal-index header from <db>-shm with a lock-safe pread and
  prove a checkpoint ran (nBackfill advanced, or the log restarted past outstanding frames).
- BoardWatch keeps the reader only for the same inode, no smaller, with that proof; it then
  drops the page cache (PRAGMA shrink_memory) and its answers, so a restore in the same interval
  is read as a new connection would read it. Every other change reopens as before.
- sync.wait/{boundary,event_wait,outbox_probe,reader_open}, sync.reader_open.step/<step>,
  sync.reader_open.reason/<why> and sync.reader_keep/checkpoint: always on, recorded as subsets
  (outer=False), so neither the step list nor sync.cpu.total/loop changes.

